       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks wrong.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the maximum adult dose.** The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily, and the maximum is 10 mg a day. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure and shock, and an amlodipine overdose is hard to reverse because the drug stays in the body for a long time.\n\nThis may be a typo for **5 mg** once daily, which is a common starting dose. Could you confirm which you meant?\n\n- **5 mg PO once daily**: I'll enter it right away.\n- **10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum): I can enter that instead.\n- **50 mg really is intended**: please confirm and give the clinical reason. Even then, this would usually need a pharmacist to review it before it's entered."
