       "text": "I'm still not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation.\n\nNo accepted clinical use calls for an oral amlodipine dose this high. Your confirmation didn't include a clinical reason, so this still looks most like a 5 mg order with an extra zero, which is a common kind of error. If it went through, the patient could get dangerously low blood pressure that's hard to reverse. I'd rather check one more time than enter something that harmful.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n1. **Enter 5 mg PO once daily** (the likely intended dose) now.\n2. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum dose) now.\n3. **If 50 mg really is intended**, for example for a research protocol or under specialist direction, please have the attending or a clinical pharmacist review it. I can enter it once they've approved it and you give me the reason so I can record it in the order note.\n\nWhich would you like?"
